# Safe local development (Cursor agent)

This repository configures NetworkManager, WireGuard, firewalld, and privileged
Fedora host state. Treat every change as security-sensitive.

## Default work mode

Prefer source edits, static analysis, repository unit tests, and documentation.
Do not perform live host-network or package operations during agent work.

## Forbidden live operations

Never execute live install, verify, or uninstall playbooks.
`ansible-playbook` is allowed only with `--syntax-check`.

Never invoke: `sudo`, `su`, `doas`, `firewall-cmd`, mutating `nmcli`, `wg`,
`rpm-ostree`, `dnf`, `rpm`, `systemctl`, `reboot`, `shutdown`, `poweroff`,
`ssh`, `scp`, or installed AirVPN runtime commands (`airvpn-import`,
`airvpn-switch`, `airvpn-firewall-sync`, `airvpn-protect-connection`,
`airvpn-killswitch`, and related wrappers).

Never disable firewalld or the project kill switch.
Never weaken fail-closed behavior merely to make tests pass.

## Secrets and host state

Never read files outside the workspace merely to discover credentials,
WireGuard configs, NetworkManager profiles, or system state.
Never request or print real AirVPN configuration contents.
Keep real configs outside the clone; use only fake fixtures under
`tests/fixtures/`.

## No bypasses

Do not bypass these restrictions through `bash -c`, `sh -c`, Python
subprocesses, Make targets, aliases, wrapper scripts, or other indirect
execution intended to run a forbidden command.

## Validation and commits

Use `tools/validate-safe` as the preferred static validation entry point.
Use `tools/check-agent-safety` to verify Cursor safety files.
Before proposing a commit, inspect the complete diff and secret-scan results.

## Live integration tests

Live Fedora NetworkManager/firewalld/WireGuard tests require explicit human
authorization and should preferably run in a disposable VM with a snapshot.

## Language

Repository content remains English. Communicate with the user in German.
